# Domain Layer — Bardak

## Repository Interfaces

Use Dart 3 `abstract interface class`. No Flutter imports allowed in domain.

```dart
abstract interface class WordPacksRepository {
  Future<WordPackInfoResultEntity> getWordPacks(GetWordPacksParams params);
  Future<bool> areWordPacksCached(AreWordPacksCachedParams params);
  Future<void> fetchAndCacheWordPacks(FetchAndCacheWordPacksParams params);
}
```

## UseCase Pattern

Simple callable class with a `call()` method. Params as a separate class in the same file.
No base `UseCase<T, P>` interface — keep it flat.

```dart
class GetWordPacksUseCase {
  const GetWordPacksUseCase(this.repository);

  final WordPacksRepository repository;

  Future<WordPackInfoResultEntity> call(GetWordPacksParams params) =>
      repository.getWordPacks(params);
}

class GetWordPacksParams {
  const GetWordPacksParams({required this.localeCode});

  final String localeCode;
}
```

Sync use cases may return plain values (no `Future`):

```dart
class GetCoinsStateUseCase {
  const GetCoinsStateUseCase(this.repository);

  final RewardsRepository repository;

  CoinBalanceEntity call() => repository.getCoinsState();
}
```

## Entities

- Pure Dart — no Flutter/data layer imports.
- Serialization (`fromJson`/`toJson`, `fromFirestore`) lives on the entity until a
  dedicated `data/models/` layer is added. Keep serialization in a named constructor /
  factory on the entity class.
- Use `copyWith` for immutable updates.
- Extend `Equatable` when used in BLoC state.

```dart
class CoinBalanceEntity extends Equatable {
  const CoinBalanceEntity({required this.coins, required this.boxesDay});

  final int coins;
  final DateTime boxesDay;

  factory CoinBalanceEntity.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) { ... }

  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() => {'coins': coins, ...};

  CoinBalanceEntity copyWith({int? coins, DateTime? boxesDay}) =>
      CoinBalanceEntity(
        coins: coins ?? this.coins,
        boxesDay: boxesDay ?? this.boxesDay,
      );

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [coins, boxesDay];
}
```

## What Belongs in Domain vs Data

| Item | Domain | Data |
|------|--------|------|
| Abstract repository | ✅ | |
| Repository impl | | ✅ |
| Entity (business rules) | ✅ | |
| DTO / Firestore mapping | ✅ (for now) | move here when adding models/ |
| Data source interface | ✅ (optional) | |
| Data source impl | | ✅ |
